1
00:00:06,230 --> 00:00:10,950
Say, Alec... About the music
I'll be performing at the Holy Night's Banquet...

2
00:00:10,950 --> 00:00:13,200
There's already a list of suggested songs...

3
00:00:13,200 --> 00:00:18,830
But I still have to narrow them down...
What kind of songs would you like, Chris?

4
00:00:22,460 --> 00:00:27,720
You're always so relaxed,
but seems like that won't fly this year, Chris.

5
00:00:28,020 --> 00:00:33,680
Once the new year comes your marriage will be drawing closer,
and you'll have a lot to do, huh?

6
00:00:33,680 --> 00:00:36,840
Alan, try not to make things more difficult for His Highness.

7
00:00:36,840 --> 00:00:38,060
All right.

8
00:00:38,580 --> 00:00:40,060
We have a serious problem!

9
00:00:42,900 --> 00:00:46,600
Alec, reject the application of the Dorud Company.

10
00:00:46,600 --> 00:00:51,200
Earl Dauner will also be involved in that one.
That may pose a challenge if we don't lay the groundwork.

11
00:00:51,200 --> 00:00:54,660
For now, the bridge over Tessen River
will take top priority

12
00:00:54,660 --> 00:00:59,120
over Earl Dauner's application for some of the budget
to be given for iron mining.

13
00:00:59,120 --> 00:01:02,330
Er... I was talking...

14
00:01:04,800 --> 00:01:07,090
Please, just listen to me.

15
00:01:07,350 --> 00:01:09,010
What's the matter?

16
00:01:09,010 --> 00:01:11,180
In accordance with the Holy Night's Banquet,

17
00:01:11,180 --> 00:01:14,890
there will be prominent families
from the Miseral Dukedom in attendance.

18
00:01:14,890 --> 00:01:17,930
What's so awful about that?

19
00:01:17,930 --> 00:01:20,600
It isn't Mintz who will be coming like usual.

20
00:01:22,690 --> 00:01:25,480
Could this be good news, then?

21
00:01:27,380 --> 00:01:28,820
Congrats, Glen!

22
00:01:28,820 --> 00:01:32,700
This isn't a joke! It will be a 10-year-old young lady!

23
00:01:36,240 --> 00:01:41,580
Above all, my mother is the most excited about it.
She's telling me how she wants a cute daughter...

24
00:01:41,580 --> 00:01:46,340
If she wants one so bad,
her and my father should get to work.

25
00:01:46,340 --> 00:01:51,220
Hold on, Glen. The prince's office is not the place
to go into your future family planning.

26
00:01:52,090 --> 00:01:54,590
Glen, Alan. Leave.

27
00:01:54,990 --> 00:01:55,730
Huh?

28
00:01:57,770 --> 00:02:03,900
Just a little while ago, Lady Eisenach was lamenting
over Glen's history of love affairs to my mother.

29
00:02:03,900 --> 00:02:05,360
You reap what you sow.

30
00:02:05,730 --> 00:02:07,730
It's about time we have more matters to discuss.

31
00:02:08,030 --> 00:02:10,990
So this is how the womanizing ends.

32
00:02:11,800 --> 00:02:16,870
Do you guys have nothing left
of that spark of youth called "friendship"?

33
00:02:17,130 --> 00:02:21,870
If you're going to help with sorting the documents,
I'd be quite happy to give you counsel.

34
00:02:22,190 --> 00:02:24,610
I don't mind either way as long as it's fun.

35
00:02:25,800 --> 00:02:31,880
<i>It seems like I'll have a hard time understanding
the friendship of gentlemen as a woman.</i>

36
00:02:32,350 --> 00:02:37,980
Joking aside, the timing of all this
does strike me as a bit too convenient.

37
00:02:41,250 --> 00:02:44,270
Lady Elianna, you have a visitor.

38
00:02:48,840 --> 00:02:51,030
If you'll excuse me, please.

39
00:02:51,860 --> 00:02:54,660
Eli, is there something bothering you?

40
00:02:57,690 --> 00:03:01,910
Well, I'm glad that everything is all right.

41
00:03:03,030 --> 00:03:05,920
<i>The "something" that His Highness mentioned...</i>

42
00:03:05,920 --> 00:03:11,170
<i>is more of a problem that I'm not accustomed to
that has become a situation recently,</i>

43
00:03:12,060 --> 00:03:17,480
<i>and that truth I cannot deny
makes my steps forward grow heavier.</i>

44
