1562
00:04:49,980 --> 00:04:56,000
A Letter From the Pearl Princess

1563
00:04:49,980 --> 00:04:56,000
A Letter From the Pearl Princess

1564
00:04:49,980 --> 00:04:56,000
A Letter From the Pearl Princess

1565
00:05:06,080 --> 00:05:09,250
We apologize for the wait, Lady Elianna!

1566
00:05:10,020 --> 00:05:11,120
Please begin.

1567
00:05:11,120 --> 00:05:15,870
Lady Elianna, today I have brought
you the precious golden pearls.

1568
00:05:15,870 --> 00:05:19,380
And I have prepared
a newly designed dress to go with it.

1569
00:05:19,380 --> 00:05:22,040
Please also take a look at this textile.

1570
00:05:22,040 --> 00:05:23,050
And this as well.

1571
00:05:23,050 --> 00:05:23,890
And this!

1572
00:05:23,890 --> 00:05:25,430
And be sure to consider this!

1573
00:05:25,430 --> 00:05:32,400
<i>My issue is, deciding on which one
from among the queen's attendants I will use...</i>

1574
00:05:34,200 --> 00:05:37,150
Lady Elianna, how about we see how they'll look on you?

1575
00:05:38,380 --> 00:05:40,050
How do you like this one?

1576
00:05:40,050 --> 00:05:41,270
Or perhaps this one?

1577
00:05:41,270 --> 00:05:43,160
Does this one suit your tastes?

1578
00:05:43,160 --> 00:05:45,410
Er, well...

1579
00:05:45,410 --> 00:05:48,370
I hope the Lady is okay.

1580
00:05:48,370 --> 00:05:53,670
Just staying at the palace until the Holy Night's Banquet is over
has her mentally exhausted.

1581
00:05:54,710 --> 00:05:58,670
Lady Elianna, has anything tickled your fancy?

1582
00:05:58,670 --> 00:05:59,970
Um...

1583
00:05:59,970 --> 00:06:03,430
If you have any suggestions, please let me know.

1584
00:06:09,860 --> 00:06:16,440
This sketch is decorated with fresh flowers,
and it's based on the Yule flowers, right?

1585
00:06:16,770 --> 00:06:18,360
That is correct.

1586
00:06:18,360 --> 00:06:23,950
Yules are, in the ancient Gaelga mythology,
a symbol of the maiden loved by the goddess.

1587
00:06:24,630 --> 00:06:32,960
While that goddess is a symbol of purity,
she is also a goddess who prefers showy colors and designs.

1588
00:06:34,330 --> 00:06:41,030
So, how about lowering the collar in imitation to that goddess' attire,

1589
00:06:41,030 --> 00:06:45,720
and adorning this part with lace
that has a Yule flower design?

1590
00:06:46,240 --> 00:06:47,350
I see!

1591
00:06:47,350 --> 00:06:51,650
Lady Elianna, please give some suggestions
to the Nash Company, as well!

1592
00:06:51,650 --> 00:06:55,750
Well. Didn't you just get some advice
from her yesterday, Nash Company?

1593
00:06:55,750 --> 00:06:59,780
Same for you, Sinus Company.
Aren't you always asking about the origins of jewels?

1594
00:06:59,780 --> 00:07:00,940
How dare you!

1595
00:07:00,940 --> 00:07:02,340
How dare <i>you</i>?!

1596
00:07:03,200 --> 00:07:04,950
Lady Elianna,

1597
00:07:04,950 --> 00:07:07,580
I think this one would suit you best!

1598
00:07:07,580 --> 00:07:09,660
I would definitely choose this one.

1599
00:07:09,660 --> 00:07:11,830
Oh no, the dazzling red is much nicer!

1600
00:07:13,910 --> 00:07:18,080
Elianna, have you still not decided on your attire?

1601
00:07:23,070 --> 00:07:26,090
I realize this is a daily occurrence,
but it's still unacceptable.

1602
00:07:26,760 --> 00:07:34,940
Elianna. The role of the crown princess is neither 
to give useful advice to merchants to earn their favor,

1603
00:07:34,940 --> 00:07:38,900
nor to pay heed to the whims of her maids.

1604
00:07:38,900 --> 00:07:40,020
Yes, Your Highness. Â

1605
00:07:40,020 --> 00:07:44,030
I want that low-cut, golden yellow dress with the flowers.

1606
00:07:44,030 --> 00:07:44,950
Yes, Your Highness!

1607
00:07:44,950 --> 00:07:48,820
Are there any fresh, original
silverwork designs for the jewelry?

1608
00:07:48,820 --> 00:07:50,370
Yes, it's right over here.

1609
00:07:51,130 --> 00:07:53,950
This won't do. Neither will this.

1610
00:07:53,950 --> 00:07:57,870
<i>I wonder if I will ever be like her? </i><i></i>

1611
00:08:06,490 --> 00:08:08,630
<i>I'm exhausted.</i>

1612
00:08:08,980 --> 00:08:12,570
Thank you so much!
We look forward to seeing you again!

1613
00:08:19,270 --> 00:08:24,030
Elianna. You are the next crown princess
of the Kingdom of Sauslind.

1614
00:08:24,480 --> 00:08:27,910
If you allow yourself to be protected by Chris
while only reading your books,

1615
00:08:28,180 --> 00:08:32,410
you're going to get yourself in trouble in critical moments.

1616
00:08:32,410 --> 00:08:33,410
Yes, Your Highness. Â

1617
00:08:34,290 --> 00:08:40,170
Once the date of your wedding is officially set,
I will not allow you to be spoiled as you have repeatedly been.

1618
00:08:41,220 --> 00:08:46,590
Once you've become a member of the royal family,
you'll need to learn to read what lies underneath a person,

1619
00:08:46,590 --> 00:08:49,680
and the art of quarreling with veteran deceivers.

1620
00:08:50,050 --> 00:08:55,110
On that point, you are socially far behind your peers.

1621
00:08:55,110 --> 00:08:58,040
But you yourself know that, yes, Elianna?

1622
00:08:58,800 --> 00:09:01,810
Yes, Queen Henrietta.

1623
00:09:02,910 --> 00:09:08,070
We just spoke of this the other day.
When it's just the two of us, what do you call me?

1624
00:09:13,100 --> 00:09:14,580
Mother.

1625
00:09:16,780 --> 00:09:24,210
Elianna, I also told you that you must not be embarrassed
every time you call me "Mother."

1626
00:09:24,210 --> 00:09:27,590
You make it sound as if
I am forcing you to use the word.

1627
00:09:27,590 --> 00:09:30,720
Yes, I sincerely apologize.

1628
00:09:32,340 --> 00:09:37,350
In any case, today there is something of great importance
I must speak to you about.

1629
00:09:38,060 --> 00:09:39,060
Yes, Your Highness. Â

1630
00:09:42,130 --> 00:09:47,860
Elianna, you remember the Ashen Nightmare
from fifteen years ago, don't you?

1631
00:09:49,110 --> 00:09:54,830
It was a plague that originated in the northeast of Sauslind
and produced a colossal amount of deaths.

1632
00:09:54,830 --> 00:09:56,370
This included your mother...

1633
00:09:57,430 --> 00:09:58,370
Right.

1634
00:09:58,370 --> 00:10:05,380
As is well-known, I also fell ill from this sickness,
and I was quarantined from the palace for a period of time.

1635
00:10:06,100 --> 00:10:09,380
At the time, Chris was at the young age of seven...

1636
00:10:09,980 --> 00:10:15,890
Since there was some time between
me marrying into the crown and Chris' birth,

1637
00:10:15,890 --> 00:10:19,650
many things were said about that by those around me.

1638
00:10:21,840 --> 00:10:24,400
You understand my intentions, right?

1639
00:10:27,400 --> 00:10:30,990
The problem facing
the current royal family of Sauslind,

1640
00:10:30,990 --> 00:10:35,280
is that the only direct heir is Prince Christopher.

1641
00:10:35,280 --> 00:10:36,450
Oh?

1642
00:10:36,450 --> 00:10:39,360
Originally, once His Highness ascends the throne,

1643
00:10:39,360 --> 00:10:44,580
the king's younger brother, His Highness Theodore,
will relinquish his rights to succession.

1644
00:10:44,580 --> 00:10:48,040
However, the king's younger brother is still in his spot.

1645
00:10:48,960 --> 00:10:53,090
In fact, the court is divided into three factions: 
those who support His Highness Theodore,

1646
00:10:53,090 --> 00:10:58,800
those who favor His Highness Christopher,
and those who remain neutral.

1647
00:11:00,110 --> 00:11:06,190
Perhaps the decision Prince Theodore himself made
to take the position of head of the royal archives,

1648
00:11:06,190 --> 00:11:11,320
the farthest position from power,
may have been made to avoid a struggle for the throne.

1649
00:11:12,390 --> 00:11:15,570
Are you saying there were some
who were promoting concubines?

1650
00:11:17,700 --> 00:11:22,690
But Queen Henrietta, what about
your support from the Miseral Dukedom?

1651
00:11:22,690 --> 00:11:27,420
That country was quite ready to offer up
one of its own duchesses to us.

1652
00:11:27,420 --> 00:11:29,040
Oh no...

1653
00:11:29,040 --> 00:11:33,590
Do you think such ideas are awful?
Or that they are too inconsiderate of me?

1654
00:11:34,120 --> 00:11:38,970
But that is the fate of women
who marry into royal families.

1655
00:11:39,970 --> 00:11:45,390
Elianna. Aside from your lack of social finesse,
more than anything else

1656
00:11:45,390 --> 00:11:48,480
you are lacking the resolve
to marry into the royal family.

1657
00:11:49,030 --> 00:11:54,230
What happened to me could happen to you so easily.

1658
00:11:54,820 --> 00:11:59,880
As the one who will stand next to Chris,
the crown prince of Sauslind,

1659
00:11:59,880 --> 00:12:02,620
do you have that determination?

1660
00:12:06,230 --> 00:12:14,510
<i>Those words were a ripple in my chest that
then became a huge wave called "anxiety"</i>

1661
00:12:14,510 --> 00:12:16,950
<i>and seemed to engulf me.</i>

1662
00:12:29,730 --> 00:12:33,740
Looks like every lady here has been completely captivated.

1663
00:12:33,740 --> 00:12:36,240
That always happens when Elen is around.

1664
00:12:36,500 --> 00:12:42,990
More importantly, Your Highness, this was a while ago,
but Glen is the one who destroyed the snow rabbit!

1665
00:12:43,360 --> 00:12:50,120
I heard that you yourself painstakingly
made it for my big sister, Mireille.

1666
00:12:50,380 --> 00:12:55,060
Lady Sharon, that was something that occurred
when I was five or six years old.

1667
00:12:55,060 --> 00:12:57,880
Maybe it was those around us who saw and remembered.

1668
00:12:58,130 --> 00:13:01,640
Oh dear, I heard it from Mireille.

1669
00:13:01,640 --> 00:13:08,770
That's one of her treasured memories with Your Highness,
and she still talks about it often.

1670
00:13:09,420 --> 00:13:11,650
<i>Miss Mireille...</i>

1671
00:13:12,860 --> 00:13:18,530
<i>She's the Grand Duchess, also known as the "Pearl Princess",
and the pride of the Miseral Dukedom,</i>

1672
00:13:18,530 --> 00:13:20,410
<i>known for her beauty and wit.</i>

1673
00:13:20,410 --> 00:13:27,910
<i>She married a countryside nobleman
and stepped down from her position as duchess.</i>

1674
00:13:27,910 --> 00:13:32,350
<i>Since she was close in age to His Highness
they spent time together when they were children. </i><i></i>

1675
00:13:32,350 --> 00:13:36,420
<i>It's even said that at one time
she was a candidate for his fiancÃ©e. </i><i></i>

1676
00:13:39,330 --> 00:13:44,640
I wish you could have invited Mireille
to the Holy Night's Banquet as well, but...

1677
00:13:44,640 --> 00:13:47,770
she's still in mourning.

1678
00:13:48,710 --> 00:13:53,440
I can't believe her husband passed
after not even two years of marriage.

1679
00:13:53,440 --> 00:13:57,520
As a citizen of an allied country, I offer my condolences.

1680
00:13:57,890 --> 00:14:04,490
I'm sure Mireille would feel better
to know of your kindness.

1681
00:14:04,490 --> 00:14:12,550
Prince Christopher, as her childhood friend, you are close to her.
Will you not help her find comfort in her grief?

1682
00:14:13,550 --> 00:14:14,670
Lady Elianna,

1683
00:14:14,990 --> 00:14:19,910
Mireilleâs aching from the loss of her husband.
Please be understanding.

1684
00:14:21,110 --> 00:14:28,010
Lady Sharon, I am sorry for her loss,
but condolences from Sauslind have already been sent.

1685
00:14:28,740 --> 00:14:35,520
If I were to be any more inconsiderate, it may bother her
as she is still immersed in memories of her husband.

1686
00:14:35,780 --> 00:14:37,060
Butâ

1687
00:14:37,400 --> 00:14:42,070
I can tell how much you want to comfort her
in her time of need.

1688
00:14:42,070 --> 00:14:48,050
Glen is a lucky man to have found
such a kind-hearted and promising partner.

1689
00:14:49,770 --> 00:14:50,950
Truly.

1690
00:14:51,510 --> 00:14:58,460
Everyone is so jealous, and they swear our house
must be under the divine protection of the marriage goddess.

1691
00:14:58,460 --> 00:15:02,460
In any case, I wonder where my son has gone off to.

1692
00:15:02,840 --> 00:15:05,760
Lady Eisenach, you're causing me some trouble as well.

1693
00:15:05,760 --> 00:15:09,180
You must have fired my mother up too
with that excitement.

1694
00:15:09,180 --> 00:15:12,180
Something about the joy
of having a daughter and so forth...

1695
00:15:12,440 --> 00:15:17,440
Forgive me for saying this, Your Highness,
but I doubt a gentleman like you would understand.

1696
00:15:17,440 --> 00:15:21,570
A daughter is a blessing from the heavens.

1697
00:15:21,570 --> 00:15:26,890
I think Eliâs appeal already speaks for itself
without you vouching for her...

1698
00:15:26,890 --> 00:15:30,580
I'd just prefer that my mother
not participate in all your gushing.

1699
00:15:30,580 --> 00:15:36,290
Well, looks like Your Highness and Lady Elianna
are quite the happy couple.

1700
00:15:36,290 --> 00:15:38,830
It's almost like the "Yule Lovers" tale.

1701
00:15:39,410 --> 00:15:41,340
The "Yule Lovers"?

1702
00:15:41,700 --> 00:15:45,970
It's an extremely popular love story
in our country right now.

1703
00:15:46,210 --> 00:15:49,720
Oh! What kind of story is it?

1704
00:15:49,720 --> 00:15:50,470
Well...

1705
00:15:52,350 --> 00:15:58,110
I think it was the love story of a prince
and the flower maiden that was loved by the goddess.

1706
00:15:58,110 --> 00:16:02,730
Let's go and see it if they make it
into a play in the future, Elianna.

1707
00:16:03,140 --> 00:16:07,490
When we go, I'll come meet you holding a Yule bouquet.

1708
00:16:08,310 --> 00:16:10,240
Y-Your Highness... um...

1709
00:16:12,120 --> 00:16:15,270
You are my precious fiancÃ©e, after all.

1710
00:16:17,490 --> 00:16:20,000
You two are the perfect pair!

1711
00:16:20,360 --> 00:16:23,920
I apologize. I must return to my official business.

1712
00:16:23,920 --> 00:16:27,510
I hope you will forgive me for leaving midway.

1713
00:16:27,740 --> 00:16:31,760
Oh no, please do what you must, Prince Christopher.

1714
00:16:33,690 --> 00:16:35,950
I'll see you afterwards, Eli.

1715
00:16:45,790 --> 00:16:49,350
<i>His Highness said he'd see me afterwards,</i>

1716
00:16:49,350 --> 00:16:53,660
<i>but I was so wrapped up in official duties
and the prince was busy with official duties,</i>

1717
00:16:53,660 --> 00:16:55,910
<i>we didn't see each other.</i>

1718
00:16:59,060 --> 00:17:04,920
I am most grateful for your invitation,
Queen Henrietta, Lady Elianna.

1719
00:17:05,300 --> 00:17:08,010
Welcome, Earl Becker.

1720
00:17:08,010 --> 00:17:10,930
It's an honor for me to meet you as well.

1721
00:17:10,930 --> 00:17:17,060
Lady Elianna. It's a shame Prince Christopher
couldn't be your escort this evening.

1722
00:17:17,060 --> 00:17:20,710
Yes. His Highness is quite busy with official business.

1723
00:17:23,500 --> 00:17:28,570
I do hope you both are in good health,
Queen Henrietta, Lady Elianna.

1724
00:17:31,220 --> 00:17:35,200
That's a signal from Queen Henrietta
that I should be wary of her.

1725
00:17:35,770 --> 00:17:40,710
How do you do, Viscountess Dauner?
And I welcome your daughter, Lady Matilda.

1726
00:17:41,220 --> 00:17:47,710
My Queen, I have had a dress
designed by my daughter tailored for tonight.

1727
00:17:47,710 --> 00:17:51,980
My daughter's dress was also designed by Matilda herself.

1728
00:17:54,820 --> 00:17:58,640
I had no idea that my daughter had such talent.

1729
00:17:59,260 --> 00:18:03,760
What do you think? May I ask your honest opinion?

1730
00:18:06,580 --> 00:18:09,150
Is that a Yule flower?

1731
00:18:10,280 --> 00:18:16,160
It may look a bit eccentric,
but the idea may have some promise.

1732
00:18:20,820 --> 00:18:23,750
Matilda is also well-versed in the history of Norn,

1733
00:18:23,750 --> 00:18:28,780
and she came up with the design of the Yule flower
which is popular over there.

1734
00:18:30,260 --> 00:18:37,220
Our family is just starting the process of negotiating
with a major company to purchase the Yule flowers.

1735
00:18:37,620 --> 00:18:42,980
I have no doubt that this will also be useful
for our relations with Norn!

1736
00:18:44,320 --> 00:18:50,730
That is promising. Lady Matilda,
would you like to play a role in diplomacy?

1737
00:18:51,330 --> 00:18:57,160
My talentless body is always humbly willing
to be of service to my country.

1738
00:18:57,160 --> 00:19:06,500
However, the best I can do is to continue the bloodline
so as not to distress the one to whom I am married.

1739
00:19:08,900 --> 00:19:13,260
My dear daughter has mastered the art of being a lady!

1740
00:19:13,700 --> 00:19:16,850
My Queen. Though this is presumptuous of me,

1741
00:19:16,850 --> 00:19:22,140
would you be willing to add my daughter's design
to Your Majesty's attire?

1742
00:19:22,530 --> 00:19:29,150
I have confidence that she will be able
to prepare something that suits Your Majesty's wishes.

1743
00:19:31,380 --> 00:19:33,110
I shall consider it.

1744
00:19:45,400 --> 00:19:47,420
It seems the insects are thriving.

1745
00:19:47,420 --> 00:19:48,960
Shall we take action?

1746
00:19:49,930 --> 00:19:50,950
Well...

1747
00:19:53,800 --> 00:19:55,880
Let's wait and see.

1748
00:19:58,470 --> 00:20:02,560
Elianna. Your hair has been mussed. Please go fix it.

1749
00:20:04,090 --> 00:20:05,150
Yes, Your Highness.

1750
00:20:06,550 --> 00:20:08,840
Please call me when you would like to return.

1751
00:20:12,170 --> 00:20:18,120
<i>Queen Henrietta has given me time to think alone.</i>

1752
00:20:18,120 --> 00:20:21,480
<i>Perhaps so I won't expose my pathetic face
on the seat of the guests of honor.</i>

1753
00:20:22,900 --> 00:20:25,160
<i>It's neither my imagination nor a coincidence...</i>

1754
00:20:25,160 --> 00:20:31,150
<i>Viscountess Dauner and her daughter's dresses
are based on a remark I made the other day. </i><i></i>

1755
00:20:32,670 --> 00:20:37,300
<i>How about adorning this part with lace
that has a Yule flower design?</i>

1756
00:20:38,000 --> 00:20:43,560
<i>This means there's someone leaking information about me.</i>

1757
00:20:46,770 --> 00:20:54,550
<i>Perhaps they think I'm not worthy of standing next
to Queen Henrietta and the prince, pathetic as I am?</i>

1758
00:21:10,330 --> 00:21:11,910
Lady Elianna?

1759
00:21:12,600 --> 00:21:15,150
I'm going to get a bit of the night breeze.

1760
00:21:26,020 --> 00:21:28,140
<i>I must keep it together.</i>

1761
00:21:28,140 --> 00:21:33,310
I think I have the answer Your Highness was seeking...

1762
00:21:33,940 --> 00:21:40,700
Me? And what question were you awaiting an answer to,
Lady Knight of Miseral?

1763
00:21:40,970 --> 00:21:46,950
If youâre angry with me, then itâs misdirected.
Iâm merely an envoy.

1764
00:21:47,420 --> 00:21:50,460
<i>She accompanied Lady Sharon...</i>

1765
00:21:51,350 --> 00:21:52,960
From Lady Mireille.

1766
00:21:54,750 --> 00:21:59,200
She is of the same opinion, Prince Christopher.

